2b0001ab	02f178f4	An idealistic young man who wanted to make a difference, Slade Wilson joined the United States Army and in time became part of an elite Army unit. After an operation he led resulted in the death of dozens of war orphans, a risk that the military leadership knew was present, he resigned. He was convinced to come back into service when the government-sponsored 'Team 7' was formed. He was told that this team was formed to deal with the increasing global trend of metahuman threats. In reality, though, the team had been formed for the express goal of establishing an American dominance in the field of 'weaponizing' humans. To that end, the team was exposed to exotic agents which brought out their latent metahuman abilities. Once this betrayal was revealed, the team dissolved and Slade committed himself to the only thing he still believed in: his family. His mission became to protect and provide for his family and in his experience only money, and a lot of it, could accomplish that.<br><br>Using his skills and metahuman abilities, Slade quickly established a name for himself as a mercenary and he became known for taking just about any mission, no questions asked. Over the years, Slade's children have become involved in his line of work, either joining him on missions or opposing him. In either case, as long as they fight well Slade is proud of them. After all, it's just business. Due to the exotic agents he was exposed to, Deathstroke possesses heightened speed, agility, reflexes and stamina. His mental abilities were enhanced as well, so that he is able to assess a situation and develop a response within a fraction of a second. There isn't a weapon that Deathstroke cannot use, but he prefers bladed weapons, especially his trademark claymore.
